                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Betham</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1749">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1839"/>
                    <occupation>Schoolmaster and Antiquary</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See ODNB - A schoolmaster in Suffolk, which might account for the pattern
                            of visits, when his antiquarian interests drew him to London. His
                            daughter Mary Matilda Betham (1776-1852) was a miniaturist and woman of
                            letters and a freind of the Lambs, Coleridge and others. But it seems
                            likely that Godwin was meeting her father. There is one Mrs Betham which
                            we have coded under this name (in 1823), alongside a 'Bethams'. Betham married Mary Planque
                            (1752/3–1839), daughter of William Damant, of Eye, Suffolk, and widow of
                            Whittocke Planque. They had fifteen children.</p>
                    </note>
